<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julius Asclepiodotus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 290–296</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Julius Asclepiodotus was a Roman praetorian prefect under the emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximian">Maximian</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-i">Constantius Chlorus</a>, and consul in 292. In 296 he led part of the invasion force that recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from the usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allectus">Allectus</a>, landing under cover of fog and defeating and killing Allectus in battle. Constantius then entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p></div>
